# BuildKit reads <dockerfile>.dockerignore in preference to the one at the
# context root, so this is the file that actually applies to
#   docker build -f apps/web/Dockerfile .
# It has to exist: the ci and build stages run `COPY . .` on top of the deps
# stage, and without **/node_modules that copy overwrites the dependencies pnpm
# just installed with whatever the host happens to have, across architectures.
# apps/web/.dockerignore holds the same rules for anyone reading the directory.

**/node_modules
**/.pnpm-store
**/.next
**/dist
**/build
**/generated
**/out
**/coverage
**/.turbo
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
**/*.tsbuildinfo

.git
.github
.vscode
.devcontainer
docs

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
certs

**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
